# {{name}}: plugin rules

A Magnusim plugin, made with `npm run plugin:new`. The host's plugin docs are
the app's `docs/plugins/` folder. Start with `docs/plugins/INDEX.md`:
`GUIDE.md` says how to build a plugin and when it is done, `DESIGN.md` how it
must look and read, and `API.md` is the reference generated from the app's code
(manifest keys, the workspace bridge, the UI kit, `magnusim_sdk`).

## Hard rules

1. Python code imports only `magnusim_sdk`, `cfddesk.registry`, the standard
   library and this plugin's own modules, and, in code that runs on its own
   environment (its service and its `python="plugin"` jobs), its lock's packages.
   `register(hub)` only declares things: import heavy packages inside the
   functions that use them.
2. The manifest's `key` is this folder's name (`{{key}}`); `api_version` is the
   host API you wrote it for (`{{api}}` here).
3. The licence is GPL-3.0-or-later, or another licence compatible with it.
{{#workspace}}
4. The workspace page gets React, the bridge (`@magnusim/workspace`) and the UI
   kit (`@magnusim/plugin-ui`) from the host's import map: never bundle them
   (`vite.config.js` marks them external, from `src/importmap.json`). A frame
   has no `localStorage`, cookies or IndexedDB: keep state in the study
   (`ws.study.update`) or the plugin's files (`ws.data`, `ws.files`).
5. Colours, sizes and fonts come from the design tokens (`var(--mg-…)`); no
   hex values outside a token.
{{/workspace}}
{{^workspace}}
4. An in-page UI (a `ui/` folder, if you add one) imports only `react`, the JSX
   runtime, `@magnusim/plugin-ui` and its own files.
5. Colours, sizes and fonts come from the design tokens (`var(--mg-…)`); no
   hex values outside a token.
{{/workspace}}
6. Use only this plugin's own data folder in a project (`magnusim_sdk.data.PluginData`,
   `ws.data`, `ws.files`).
7. Job tools live in this folder (`tools/`); a `[python]` lock pins every package
   with `==` and a `--hash`.
8. No placeholder copy: no "coming soon", `TODO` or "lorem" in anything that ships.
   Every button works end to end, and every action tells the user what happened.

## Layout

| Path | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `manifest.toml` | What the host reads before importing anything |
| `plugin.py` | `register(hub)`: declares {{#workspace}}its job{{^service}} and backend method{{/service}}{{/workspace}}{{^workspace}}the analysis it adds{{/workspace}} |
{{#service}}| `service/` | Its backend, run by `magnusim_sdk.service` in its own environment |
{{/service}}{{#job}}| `tools/` | Job tools; they report progress with `magnusim_sdk.events.emit` |
{{/job}}{{#venv}}| `requirements.lock` | Its own environment's packages, pinned and hashed |
{{/venv}}{{#workspace}}| `src/` | The workspace page's source (`npm run build` writes `workspace/`) |
| `workspace/` | What the host serves in the sandboxed frame (built; committed) |
| `types/` | The bridge's and the kit's types, copied from the app's `docs/plugins/` |
{{/workspace}}| `tests/` | pytest tests{{#workspace}}, and `tests/e2e/` for the browser{{/workspace}} |

## Check it

From the app folder:

```
npm run plugin:check -- {{check_path}}
```

It runs every rule above and this plugin's own pytest tests. To run pytest
alone, from the app folder, on the app's interpreter:
`python/.venv/Scripts/python -m pytest {{check_path}}/tests`.{{#workspace}} The
browser test needs the app: `npx playwright test -c {{e2e_config}}`. After
changing `src/`, run `npm install` and `npm run build` in this folder: the host
serves `workspace/`, not `src/`.{{/workspace}}

Done means: the real flow works end to end in the app, `plugin:check` passes,
every bug found has a test, turning the plugin off leaves no trace, and removing
it keeps the studies it made.
